From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h700: drop the 1512 MHz CPU OPP

The H616 OPP table tops out at 1512 MHz (1.16 V for the speed bin the
H700 reports, the vdd-cpu limit). Under a sustained load at that point the
RG CubeXX corrupts page tables and user memory: rsync copies die with
SIGILL or hang, the kernel reports "Bad page map" with PTEs carrying stray
high bits and oopses with level 3 address size faults. Measured from a
clean boot (10 rsync runs of 440 MB each): 1512 MHz 2 failed + 4 kernel
errors; 1416 MHz, 1200 MHz and 1008 MHz 0 failed, 0 errors. Remove the
1512 MHz point from the H700 family base so every board stops at 1416 MHz.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
@@ -12,6 +12,16 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 
+/*
+ * The H616 1512 MHz operating point is not stable on the H700: under a
+ * sustained load (rsync, an SD2 restore) it corrupts page tables and user
+ * memory (bad page map, SIGILL, kernel oops) on the RG CubeXX, while 1416
+ * MHz and below run clean. The H700 tops out at 1416 MHz.
+ */
+&cpu_opp_table {
+	/delete-node/ opp-1512000000;
+};
+
 / {
 	model = "Anbernic RG35XX 2024";
 	chassis-type = "handset";
